    "updated_at": "2025-04-22T16:38:07Z",
    "body": "Ya I think allowing the user to pass a solver function might be nice. It would allow interfacing different solvers as you mention, and it would also kick the problem of parallelizing your batches to the user. If the user doesn't pass anything, we can just use pyscf serially (or with python multiprocessing) internally.\n\n```\ndef my_callable_solver(batches, hcore, eri, ...) -> Sequence[Tuple[float, SCIState, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"Take in batches and integrals, return solutions for each batch.\"\"\"\n    ...\n\n...\n... = run_sqd(..., my_callable_solver, ...)\n```\n\nWhat do you think?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
